  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Learning is now part of your profession. Not an occasional activity. Not something reserved for courses and certificates. A daily practice.",
      "start": 1.159,
      "end": 9.579,
      "word_start": 0,
      "word_end": 20
    },
    {
      "text": "The world changes too quickly for any fixed body of knowledge to protect you forever. What matters is the speed at which you can encounter something unfamiliar, understand it, test it, and make it useful.",
      "start": 10.42,
      "end": 23.979,
      "word_start": 21,
      "word_end": 55
    },
    {
      "text": "Read every day. Build while you learn. Take notes in your own words. Explain difficult ideas simply. Follow curiosity beyond the point where it stops being convenient.",
      "start": 24.979,
      "end": 36.159,
      "word_start": 56,
      "word_end": 82
    },
    {
      "text": "You will often feel as though everybody else understands more than you do. They do not. They have merely been confused for longer.",
